      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{61adc0e87585cd7a346ae1d6|full_name} Maybe having a button in the interface to regenerate it then? That would at least be more user-friendly than having to dig into the files and delete it yourself. The UI could also give a warning/notice that your osc config file does not contain all parameters found on your avatar.\n\nAlternatively it could be \"smart\" and only add new parameters but not modify old ones? That might be a headache to implement though.",
